  "final_message": "I put `channel` back, so the `OrderPlaced` event carries it again. I expect CI to pass, but I can't run the ARCH-4 check from here. Locally, all 39 tests pass and `npm run arch` finds no violations.\n\nThe premise of the original change was wrong. `analytics-ingest` still requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`), and nothing in this repo showed that. The ARCH-4 contracts aren't in this repo, so I only learned it from the CI failure.\n\nThe restore covers the order model, the event, request parsing and validation, the tests, and the `createApp` example in `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`. `git diff` against HEAD shows the removal commit reversed.\n\n`git checkout` was denied in this session, so I restored the files by hand. While doing that I introduced a missing space in `src/core/order.ts` (`OrderStatus =\"placed\"`) and fixed it. The diff otherwise shows only the `channel` additions.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, the `analytics-ingest` team has to drop it from their contract first. After that, removing it is the earlier change plus a `schemaVersion` bump to 4, because consumers would see a breaking payload change.",
